  "worked_solution": "Since $u=x-1,$ then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n$x=u+1.$\n\nNow we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\sqrt[5]{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (u+1)(\\sqrt[5]{u})(\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int (u+1)({u}^{1/5})(\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int ({u}^{6/5}+{u}^{1/5})\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$",
